's a comprehensive design for cursor-based pagination in a REST API:

## 1. Endpoint Shape

### Request Format
```
GET /api/resource?cursor={encoded_cursor}&limit=20
```

### Response Format
```json
{
  "data": [...],
  "pagination": {
    "next_cursor": "encoded_string_or_null",
    "has_more": true/false
  }
}
```

## 2. Cursor Encoding

ds4: CUDA loading model tensors 7.86 GiB cached
### Recommended Approach: Base64-encoded JSON

```javascript
// Encoding
function encodeCursor(cursorData) {
  const json = JSON.stringify(cursorData);
  return Buffer.from(json).toString('base64url');
}

// Decoding
function decodeCursor(cursorString) {
  const json = Buffer.from(cursorString, 'base64url').toString();
  return JSON.parse(json);
}
```

### Cursor Structure
```json
{
  "last_seen_id": "12345",
  "last_seen_value": "2024-01-15T12:00:00Z",
  "sort_field": "created_at",
  "direction": "asc"
}
```

